WEBVTT

00:00.840 --> 00:07.150
So, Father, about what I was saying concerning
humans and monsters living together...

00:07.550 --> 00:12.390
The main issue is that the monsters 
are losing their places to live, right?

00:12.390 --> 00:14.610
So we just have to make new places.

00:15.010 --> 00:16.060
Hmm...

00:17.140 --> 00:19.800
We could put up a barrier 
on a mountain where no one lives,

00:19.800 --> 00:23.180
then have all the monsters who've 
lost their homes move in there.

00:23.180 --> 00:27.490
And if the monsters overpopulate,

00:27.490 --> 00:31.120
we'll make it a training area
 for the adventurers' guild

00:31.480 --> 00:35.850
We can cover the expenses by placing inns 
and shops at the base of the mountain.

00:35.850 --> 00:40.010
Then we'll have adventurers and monsters
keep each other in check.

00:40.010 --> 00:41.310
What do you think?

00:41.310 --> 00:43.810
<i>Talk about the most cliché RPG setup...</i>

00:44.060 --> 00:47.420
We'd run the risk of the monsters
 killing humans that way...

00:47.420 --> 00:49.200
Yes, and the opposite too.

00:49.200 --> 00:51.540
But that's all a part 
of the struggle to survive,

00:51.540 --> 00:54.620
and we can explain as much
 to the adventurers.

00:54.620 --> 00:55.760
I see.

00:56.360 --> 00:59.340
This plan is rather naïve,
 but I'll give it some thought.

01:01.100 --> 01:02.450
Thank you.

01:04.690 --> 01:06.780
<i>Maybe I'll scout some potential locations</i>

01:06.780 --> 01:09.540
<i>for my plan while we're on this inspection.</i>

01:18.760 --> 01:23.680
<b><i>Fluffy Paradise</i></b>

02:40.300 --> 02:45.510
<b><i>Episode 7   I Believe I Can Be of Some Service</i></b>

02:40.350 --> 02:43.890
Now then, we'll be heading
 to our next inspection destination,

02:43.890 --> 02:45.840
and I'd like for you to come, Shinki.

02:46.920 --> 02:49.650
Your elemental powers may be a great help,

02:49.650 --> 02:51.780
and you must be knowledgeable 
about monsters.

02:53.810 --> 02:58.380
I don't mind going, but I'm worried 
about leaving the nest for too long.

02:58.920 --> 03:03.110
<i>I'm the one with the orb, and we 
can't keep that barrier up forever.</i>

03:03.560 --> 03:05.340
All right. How about this?

03:05.860 --> 03:08.280
We'll have these spirits protect the nest.

03:08.680 --> 03:12.670
Master, please give the next 
strongest goblin a name.

03:12.980 --> 03:17.550
Then they can protect the nest 
alongside the spirits, and I can rest easy.

03:17.550 --> 03:19.940
Huh?! Why me?!

03:19.940 --> 03:22.120
Also, why did you just call me "Master"?!

03:22.340 --> 03:26.340
Well, you're my master since you named me,
 which makes you the leader of our horde.

03:27.660 --> 03:29.830
<i>But Shinki is a friend.</i>

03:29.830 --> 03:32.300
<i>And being called "Master" 
is really embarrassing.</i>

03:32.640 --> 03:34.780
Can't you just treat me like a lady?

03:34.780 --> 03:37.770
Very well. I shall call you 
my lady from now on.

03:42.480 --> 03:45.180
She's the next strongest goblin after you?

03:45.180 --> 03:45.790
She is.

03:46.080 --> 03:47.880
<i>I'm surprised it's a girl!</i>

03:47.880 --> 03:49.360
Leader... you called?

03:49.360 --> 03:51.040
She can talk?!

03:51.040 --> 03:54.700
Yes. She's my right hand.

03:55.260 --> 03:58.370
She'll probably evolve
 after a few more hunting trips.

03:58.370 --> 04:00.280
<i>She'll evolve...?</i>

04:02.670 --> 04:06.670
<i>No, maybe female hobgoblins are cute.</i>

04:08.490 --> 04:10.830
Let's give you a cute name, okay?

04:13.890 --> 04:16.310
So, what do you like?

04:23.440 --> 04:25.830
You like flowers?

04:25.830 --> 04:27.070
<i>I see...</i>

04:27.990 --> 04:30.080
<i>That looks like a lily of the valley,
 or suzuran.</i>

04:30.400 --> 04:33.500
Suzuko! Your name's Suzuko.

04:33.900 --> 04:36.450
Su...zu...ko?

04:36.450 --> 04:38.450
Yup, you got it!

04:42.380 --> 04:45.960
Yay! From now on, you're Suzuko!

04:51.420 --> 04:54.500
My lady, he would like a name as well.

04:55.880 --> 04:59.170
No! He's weak! No!

05:01.020 --> 05:02.860
Why does he want a name?

05:05.630 --> 05:06.080
Ah...

05:06.690 --> 05:10.290
Apparently, his last horde 
was all but wiped out.

05:10.810 --> 05:15.620
He says he'd like to be stronger
so that he can protect his current one.

05:16.530 --> 05:19.770
But just as Suzuko pointed out, he's weak.

05:19.770 --> 05:22.830
There's not much hope for him
 even if he gets a name.

05:22.830 --> 05:24.100
Oh no...

05:25.640 --> 05:29.130
<i>But giving up on him because 
he may not grow is kinda...</i>

05:29.560 --> 05:33.610
Okay, if you can keep this promise,
 I'll give you a name.

05:33.860 --> 05:39.060
You must be able to hunt giant boars 
by yourself by the time we come back.

05:39.350 --> 05:43.590
You're so small that you could die 
if they happen to body slam you.

05:43.590 --> 05:45.510
There's no guarantee you'll survive.

05:45.510 --> 05:47.030
Would you work hard even so?

05:47.390 --> 05:50.100
<i>Honestly, this is partly a threat.</i>

05:50.100 --> 05:52.240
<i>I'll get to see if he's serious.</i>

05:55.030 --> 05:56.560
Then I guess it's decided!

05:56.560 --> 06:00.420
<i>As for a name that suits him 
and will hopefully make him stronger...</i>

06:00.760 --> 06:01.970
Hmm...

06:01.970 --> 06:05.140
<i>I know! Let's go with Touki, 
which means "fighting ogre"!</i>

06:04.920 --> 06:06.130
<b>TOUKI</b>

06:06.120 --> 06:08.700
Your name will be Touki!

06:13.150 --> 06:15.060
Let's both do our best.

06:18.840 --> 06:23.180
And then, I gave Sol head pats 
because I summoned him by accident.

06:23.180 --> 06:25.820
That's how we got so close!

06:26.160 --> 06:29.650
You're surrounded by so many 
people and creatures, my lady.

06:29.650 --> 06:30.290
Yes!

06:30.530 --> 06:35.010
Father, Mother, 
my big brother, my big sister,

06:35.010 --> 06:40.490
Dee, Nox, everyone at home, 
and everyone at the palace...

06:40.810 --> 06:42.450
I love them all!

06:43.200 --> 06:48.040
I had an older brother as well... 
Though he died battling the humans.

06:49.270 --> 06:50.500
<i>Shinki...</i>

06:53.080 --> 06:56.180
You're part of my circle
of friends now too, Shinki.

07:00.970 --> 07:03.350
Thank you, my lady.

07:05.950 --> 07:09.160
We're headed to the town
of Cass in the Parzeth Proxy next.

07:09.450 --> 07:11.670
It'll take a while to get there,

07:11.670 --> 07:15.510
so I was hoping you'd be able
 to enlighten us on the way, Shinki.

07:16.230 --> 07:17.710
All right.

07:17.710 --> 07:21.570
I'm currently compiling eyewitness 
reports of monsters.

07:22.100 --> 07:26.370
Could you tell me about the route 
you traveled as you were fleeing?

07:26.850 --> 07:30.230
I'd be interested in any
 of its defining features.

07:31.330 --> 07:34.860
Far down the path, there were 
three connecting mountains.

07:35.180 --> 07:37.100
I see. Mountains, you say?

07:37.100 --> 07:39.090
And a very rough river.

07:39.760 --> 07:41.050
Got it.

07:41.760 --> 07:45.390
Thank you.
I think I've managed to sort this out.

07:46.030 --> 07:49.770
These mark all the recent reported sightings.

07:50.540 --> 07:51.490
Huh?

07:51.490 --> 07:53.930
<i>The Osphe domain is bleeding red!</i>

07:53.930 --> 07:57.870
I can't be certain until I 
gather more information,

07:57.870 --> 08:01.320
but this trouble with the monsters 
may be man-made.

08:01.740 --> 08:04.800
We need to investigate thoroughly.

08:05.320 --> 08:08.090
I'm sorry, but after the inspection in Cass,

08:08.090 --> 08:09.970
I shall return to the royal capital.

08:09.970 --> 08:11.510
What? You're going home?

08:11.940 --> 08:13.160
<i>Why?!</i>

08:13.160 --> 08:16.380
<i>I wanted to scout out locations for my plan!</i>

08:16.380 --> 08:18.300
I've asked Ralf to come fill in for me.

08:19.080 --> 08:20.370
<i>Ralf?!</i>

08:20.370 --> 08:22.220
He'll eventually take over the domain,

08:22.220 --> 08:24.980
so I'm having him make
 the rounds on my behalf.

08:25.410 --> 08:28.130
You should be able to meet 
up with him in Cass.

08:29.150 --> 08:30.700
Look, we can see it now.

08:31.050 --> 08:32.910
This is the town of Cass.

08:35.410 --> 08:37.990
Thank you for coming!

08:37.990 --> 08:40.880
You must be tired from your 
long journey. Right this way.

08:41.110 --> 08:44.650
<i>There's somewhere I want to see...</i>

08:41.340 --> 08:43.100
We've a meal prepared for you.

08:43.100 --> 08:45.070
Please, come with us.

08:45.070 --> 08:47.080
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

08:47.300 --> 08:50.310
<i>There! A sign for the adventurers' guild!</i>

08:50.310 --> 08:53.260
<i>They'll be helping me out with my plan,</i>

08:53.260 --> 08:55.340
<i>so I wanted to check them out.</i>

08:57.550 --> 09:00.090
<i>This definitely isn't what I was imagining.</i>

09:00.090 --> 09:03.150
<i>Sorta looks like an employment 
agency from my past life.</i>

09:04.310 --> 09:07.470
Hello there. How can I help you?

09:09.390 --> 09:11.190
O-Oh my...

09:12.420 --> 09:14.500
<i>Does she know Shinki's a monster?!</i>

09:14.860 --> 09:17.710
Beastpeople aren't common in these parts,

09:17.710 --> 09:20.350
so you might not want to linger for long.

09:20.350 --> 09:23.160
<i>She has no idea! We're safe.</i>

09:23.160 --> 09:25.200
I'll leave as soon as my lady is done here.

09:25.490 --> 09:28.240
W-Wait, your <i>lady</i>? This young girl?

09:28.920 --> 09:30.410
<i>Yeah, I get that reaction.</i>

09:30.840 --> 09:35.780
My apologies. I just wanted to see 
what the guild hall looked like.

09:35.780 --> 09:37.640
You don't have one where you're from?

09:38.070 --> 09:41.600
The guild hall in the royal capital 
is far from where I live,

09:41.600 --> 09:43.440
so I don't really get to go there.

09:43.440 --> 09:45.220
Ah, I see.

09:45.870 --> 09:48.200
Then I'll show you around a little.

09:48.200 --> 09:51.520
My name is Ariabelle, 
but you can call me Belle.

09:51.790 --> 09:55.800
I'm Neema, and this is Shinki!
 Nice to meet you!

09:57.690 --> 10:00.140
These are our private reception booths.

10:00.140 --> 10:03.440
We offer various quests to our 
adventurers based on their ranks.

10:04.010 --> 10:08.860
To make sure no one overhears the details,
we use soundproofing magic.

10:08.860 --> 10:09.660
You do?

10:09.970 --> 10:12.430
Apparently when the guild 
was first established,

10:12.430 --> 10:14.760
reward swiping was rampant.

10:15.180 --> 10:15.830
Huh?

10:16.180 --> 10:21.600
Folks would cash in on quests other
adventurers had completed for the reward

10:21.920 --> 10:25.430
because more than one person 
could take a job.

10:25.740 --> 10:27.610
<i>That's so evil!</i>

10:27.830 --> 10:30.470
Of course, it becomes a trust issue.

10:30.470 --> 10:33.430
Who wants anyone who does that
to call themselves an adventurer?

10:34.060 --> 10:37.260
So, ever since then,
we've used magic to prevent it.

10:37.260 --> 10:40.370
The adventurers' guild is very 
strict about wrongdoing.

10:40.370 --> 10:41.980
Oho...

10:41.980 --> 10:43.830
<i>I guess things are better now.</i>

10:45.360 --> 10:46.710
What's that supposed to mean?!

10:46.980 --> 10:50.470
Is the guild just going to sit by 
and ignore this injustice?!

10:50.800 --> 10:53.250
<i>Wh-What in the world?</i>

10:54.830 --> 10:58.180
Is the guild just going to sit by 
and ignore this injustice?!

10:58.730 --> 11:02.340
Three times the standard reward 
just to clear a small goblin horde?

11:02.340 --> 11:05.700
The mayor put this job up
and his son accepted it!

11:03.150 --> 11:05.700
<i>Wh-What about the soundproofing magic?</i>

11:05.700 --> 11:08.680
<i>I guess he's yelling outside the booth...</i>

11:05.700 --> 11:09.070
Clearly, the mayor is just 
lining his own pockets!

11:09.070 --> 11:12.100
The mayor is just doing 
what's best for the town...

11:12.100 --> 11:13.510
What are you saying?!

11:13.510 --> 11:17.250
He's pocketing the restitution for
any casualties caused by monsters!

11:17.630 --> 11:20.190
<i>This all sounds really fishy...</i>

11:20.520 --> 11:22.500
Why isn't anyone taking this seriously?!

11:20.700 --> 11:24.100
Miss Belle, who is that?

11:25.170 --> 11:27.240
His name is Healran Dewitt.

11:25.510 --> 11:27.230
What's going on?!

11:27.230 --> 11:29.510
I'm not sure what else I can say...

11:27.240 --> 11:28.910
He's one of the town chairmen.

11:28.910 --> 11:32.110
He's very good at his job
but doesn't get along with the mayor.

11:32.110 --> 11:34.370
Please, calm down.

11:32.550 --> 11:35.440
Can't the guild do something?

11:35.440 --> 11:38.290
Most of the staff are locals,

11:38.290 --> 11:40.340
so when they're told it's best for the town...

11:40.850 --> 11:44.190
<i>They're supposedly strict on wrongdoing, 
but this place is so small</i>

11:44.190 --> 11:46.300
<i>that they go easy on one of their own...</i>

11:46.570 --> 11:50.410
Apparently, he used to work at the palace.

11:50.410 --> 11:53.740
Maybe that's why he just
 can't let stuff like this slide.

11:54.210 --> 11:57.600
<i>He's from the palace?
What's he doing out here in the country?</i>

12:00.740 --> 12:06.360
Please, you're going to disturb others 
 out here, so kindly return to the booth.

12:06.360 --> 12:08.700
But if we turn a blind eye...

12:13.350 --> 12:16.540
Could you tell me more about it, sir?

12:18.820 --> 12:20.570
I've no time for children.

12:20.570 --> 12:23.810
<i>Wh-What'd he just say?!</i>

12:23.810 --> 12:26.050
Ahem. Oh, I see.

12:26.050 --> 12:30.200
And here I thought I could be
 of some service, but oh well.

12:31.550 --> 12:33.150
What do you mean by that?

12:33.150 --> 12:33.880
Eek!

12:35.570 --> 12:37.350
I know the duke of this domain...

12:37.680 --> 12:39.570
<i>You</i> know the duke?

12:41.260 --> 12:43.630
My name is Nefertima Osphe.

12:43.630 --> 12:45.990
I'm the second daughter of Dayland Osphe.

12:46.620 --> 12:49.960
Depending on what it is, I may be able 
to relay this matter to my father.

12:49.960 --> 12:51.240
What do you say?

12:51.800 --> 12:52.840
Wha...

12:52.840 --> 12:55.030
You're the duke's daughter?!

12:55.580 --> 12:58.190
<i>Well, let's hear it.</i>

12:58.190 --> 13:02.320
<i>What exactly is going on in this town?</i>

13:04.440 --> 13:07.010
I apologize for my rudeness earlier.

13:07.520 --> 13:12.970
I'm Healran Dewitt, 
the financial auditor of this town.

13:13.430 --> 13:15.530
<i>The financial auditor?</i>

13:15.530 --> 13:19.300
<i>The guy who makes sure all financial
accounts and reports are done right?</i>

13:19.550 --> 13:23.760
Let's get right down to business. 
Can you tell me more about the mayor?

13:24.240 --> 13:25.570
I beg your pardon,

13:25.570 --> 13:28.410
but this may be difficult
 for someone your age to follow.

13:29.530 --> 13:31.610
<i>Yeah, I can't blame him for thinking that.</i>

13:31.970 --> 13:36.200
Well, I'm smart enough to accompany
 my father on inspections.

13:36.570 --> 13:42.290
Very well. Are you aware of the steep 
rise in monster attacks lately?

13:42.290 --> 13:43.090
Yes.

13:43.400 --> 13:46.850
There's been an increase
 in the Parzeth Proxy as well,

13:46.850 --> 13:49.920
but in Cass specifically,
we've barely had more than last year.

13:50.480 --> 13:54.350
A few people have been injured,
but the mayor grossly exaggerates.

13:54.350 --> 13:56.870
He made false reports claiming fatalities,

13:56.870 --> 14:00.380
and he pocketed the five gold 
coins sent as restitution.

14:00.380 --> 14:04.470
<i>Five gold coins? So about five million yen?</i>

14:04.470 --> 14:08.650
<i>Okay, so we're dealing with your 
typical small-time villain.</i>

14:08.650 --> 14:10.300
Have you beseeched the knights?

14:10.300 --> 14:12.000
When there were goblin sightings,

14:12.000 --> 14:14.310
we sent out a subjugation 
request immediately,

14:14.310 --> 14:16.880
but for certain reasons, 
the knights couldn't come.

14:16.880 --> 14:18.200
<i>Certain reasons?</i>

14:18.200 --> 14:20.550
That was when the townsfolk were harmed.

14:21.370 --> 14:26.220
Beyond that, the mayor's been doing things
like inflating the cost of infrastructure.

14:26.940 --> 14:30.190
Have you any proof of this?

14:30.190 --> 14:34.390
Yes. I've witnessed him gleefully 
keeping a secret ledger.

14:34.700 --> 14:40.080
<i>Yeesh, okay. Well, as long as there's 
evidence, the rest is up to Papa.</i>

14:40.080 --> 14:42.930
Would you swear on your name to as much

14:42.930 --> 14:44.730
and repeat it before my father?

14:46.840 --> 14:47.720
Yes!

14:49.950 --> 14:51.590
Very well.

14:51.590 --> 14:53.610
I have but one concern.

14:53.610 --> 14:58.700
Do you happen to know why the 
knighthood couldn't make it here?

14:58.700 --> 15:03.840
Yes. West of here lies the biggest 
city in the Parzeth Proxy, Lenice.

15:04.580 --> 15:09.420
The Manoa Highway runs through it
and is integral to trade,

15:09.420 --> 15:13.180
but it's been hit relentlessly 
by kobold robberies.

15:13.490 --> 15:14.640
<i>Kobolds?!</i>

15:14.900 --> 15:17.650
And that's what's keeping them busy?

15:17.650 --> 15:19.650
The kobolds are many in number

15:19.650 --> 15:22.300
and move in a very organized manner.

15:22.300 --> 15:25.870
At one point, Lenice itself was in danger.

15:25.870 --> 15:30.910
So most of the knights in this region have 
been deployed and are unable to come.

15:32.550 --> 15:34.200
Lady Nefertima?

15:34.630 --> 15:37.800
<i>If they're organized, 
that must mean they have a leader.</i>

15:37.800 --> 15:42.350
<i>If all goes well, I may be able to pull 
in the kobolds into my plan, too!</i>

15:42.860 --> 15:45.790
Yes! We welcome the puppers!

15:46.130 --> 15:48.010
What does "welcome the puppers" mean?

15:48.520 --> 15:51.140
Huh?! Hey, don't go reading my mind!

15:51.140 --> 15:52.500
You said that <i>very</i> out loud.

15:53.030 --> 15:59.120
Ahem, anyway... Healran, you should 
come with me to see my father.

15:59.120 --> 16:00.220
R-Right.

16:00.690 --> 16:02.700
I have a favor to ask, Shinki.

16:03.450 --> 16:07.430
I need you to convince the goblin hordes
 around here to do something.

16:07.430 --> 16:08.610
Of what?

16:08.610 --> 16:12.940
To join you... Or rather, 
to band together under Suzuko.

16:13.380 --> 16:14.160
Understood.

16:14.770 --> 16:16.250
Also...

16:17.930 --> 16:19.250
Nox.

16:19.250 --> 16:20.320
Cheep.

16:21.620 --> 16:22.840
Cheep.

16:22.840 --> 16:24.670
There, there. Good girl.

16:25.090 --> 16:28.870
Find Father for me and give him this message.

16:28.870 --> 16:29.510
Cheep.

16:30.970 --> 16:31.780
Cheep!

16:31.780 --> 16:34.810
Make sure he comes to the mayor's house!

16:35.240 --> 16:38.610
Um, you're going to the mayor's place, then?

16:38.610 --> 16:40.140
I can take you there.

16:40.510 --> 16:44.110
But this isn't part of your job, Miss Belle.

16:44.110 --> 16:47.360
As a part of this town, 
I want to help somehow.

16:47.960 --> 16:50.820
All right. In that case, I'm counting on you!

16:52.190 --> 16:55.770
Has the mayor been in office for a long time?

16:55.770 --> 17:00.310
Yes. I believe he's been the mayor since he 
took over for the last one fifteen years ago.

17:00.310 --> 17:03.180
I wonder how long he's been embezzling...

17:03.180 --> 17:05.510
I believe it started about five years ago.

17:06.000 --> 17:06.960
<i>Oh?</i>

17:06.960 --> 17:09.220
I'm surprised you'd know that.

17:09.220 --> 17:13.160
Didn't you only come to town three years ago?

17:13.540 --> 17:16.230
Well, I checked past records.

17:16.230 --> 17:19.800
Apparently my predecessor
didn't do their job properly.

17:20.210 --> 17:24.520
<i>Wow, I guess he really is adamant.</i>

17:24.780 --> 17:28.590
You can see it now. That's the mayor's house.

17:28.590 --> 17:30.420
Nox is there, too!

17:30.420 --> 17:32.230
Which means...

17:35.390 --> 17:37.640
Wandering off without permission...

17:37.640 --> 17:41.010
If you've got an excuse, 
let's hear it, Nefertima.

17:41.010 --> 17:42.860
<i>Angry Papa has arrived!</i>

17:43.190 --> 17:47.330
<i>I-I... should probably be honest 
and apologize here, right?</i>

17:47.810 --> 17:50.210
I'm sorry I worried you!

17:50.210 --> 17:53.110
I'm sorry for causing everyone trouble, too!

17:53.110 --> 17:56.570
I wanted to see the adventurers' guild.

17:56.570 --> 17:57.760
Where's Shinki?

17:57.760 --> 18:00.580
He went to see the goblins causing trouble.

18:02.390 --> 18:03.860
Nefertima...

18:03.860 --> 18:07.740
Do you have any idea how 
foolishly you've behaved?

18:08.280 --> 18:13.100
It may have been too early to present 
you to the world as a duke's daughter.

18:14.310 --> 18:15.470
<i>Papa...</i>

18:15.820 --> 18:17.730
<i>Up until now,</i>

18:17.730 --> 18:21.730
<i>he'd tell me something was dangerous 
or decline my request with good reason.</i>

18:21.730 --> 18:26.090
<i>But I've never seen him 
this upset with me before.</i>

18:27.230 --> 18:29.750
<i>No! Papa has every right to be mad!</i>

18:30.110 --> 18:33.440
<i>The point of this trip was to observe
 various parts of his domain.</i>

18:33.440 --> 18:36.460
<i>Even if I'm just tagging along, 
I'm part of his party.</i>

18:37.250 --> 18:40.040
<i>And yet, not only did I run 
off without his permission,</i>

18:40.040 --> 18:42.090
<i>I didn't even keep my guard with me.</i>

18:42.910 --> 18:44.650
<i>If something had happened to me,</i>

18:44.650 --> 18:48.310
<i>the ones who would've punished were 
those tasked to protect me.</i>

18:48.310 --> 18:51.140
<i>How could I do something so selfish?</i>

18:51.540 --> 18:54.810
<i>Your status should be used 
to protect those below you.</i>

18:54.810 --> 18:56.600
<i>That's what I've been taught...</i>

18:59.770 --> 19:03.900
Now, now, Father. Not even you 
are allowed to make Neema cry.

19:04.270 --> 19:05.860
Ralf?

19:06.230 --> 19:10.070
He can scold us both together, 
so don't you worry.

19:10.350 --> 19:13.030
Ralf! You made it here so soon?

19:13.030 --> 19:15.500
<i>Ah, that's right...</i>

19:15.880 --> 19:19.740
<i>My older brother and sister 
always take my side.</i>

19:19.740 --> 19:23.840
<i>No matter how wrong I am, 
they always take the scolding with me.</i>

19:24.170 --> 19:28.250
<i>Oh no. Now that the nerves have passed, 
the tears and snot won't stop...</i>

19:30.060 --> 19:31.270
Here, use this.

19:31.580 --> 19:33.540
Th-Thanks—

19:35.890 --> 19:37.340
What was that for?!

19:39.530 --> 19:40.280
Will?!

19:40.610 --> 19:41.790
Wh-Wha...

19:42.870 --> 19:43.980
<i>Lars?</i>

19:47.220 --> 19:49.340
Good evening, Prince Wilhert.

19:50.180 --> 19:51.230
The prince?!

19:51.230 --> 19:51.840
What?!

19:55.710 --> 19:57.720
It's all right. At ease.

19:59.480 --> 20:01.800
Your Highness, what brings you here?

20:01.800 --> 20:04.020
I just wrapped up some business,

20:04.020 --> 20:07.390
so I thought I'd play with 
Nefertima and relax a bit,

20:07.390 --> 20:10.010
but Ralf told me she was accompanying you.

20:10.380 --> 20:12.730
Does His Majesty know you're here?

20:12.730 --> 20:14.850
Yes. I've brought guards with me.

20:15.160 --> 20:20.830
Very well. But if His Majesty asks 
you to return, please do so.

20:21.300 --> 20:23.730
<i>Papa's definitely not smiling on the inside.</i>

20:24.030 --> 20:27.320
By the way, Neema, who are these people?

20:27.320 --> 20:29.120
Oh, right!

20:30.060 --> 20:33.070
This is Healran,
this town's financial auditor.

20:33.070 --> 20:36.350
And this is Miss Ariabelle,
who helped me at the guild.

20:36.670 --> 20:40.930
There's something that Healran 
would like to tell you, Father.

20:41.230 --> 20:43.620
He needs your help!

20:44.360 --> 20:46.410
If that's the case,

20:46.410 --> 20:49.460
it must be either as the
 duke or the prime minister.

20:49.810 --> 20:51.490
Yes, Your Grace.

20:51.490 --> 20:56.490
I'd like to speak with you
 about the mayor's embezzling.

20:56.940 --> 20:57.870
What?!

20:58.710 --> 21:00.930
Very well. Let us talk inside.

21:02.380 --> 21:04.610
Oh, Your Grace!

21:04.610 --> 21:06.900
Sorry for taking off.

21:07.140 --> 21:10.140
Were you able to meet 
with your acquaintance?

21:10.140 --> 21:11.620
Yes, I was...

21:12.110 --> 21:15.060
But apparently, these people 
have something to say to you.

21:15.450 --> 21:17.950
What's this I hear about embezzlement?

21:19.850 --> 21:23.190
<i>After that, the adults had 
a very difficult conversation</i>

21:23.190 --> 21:27.930
<i>about the mayor's embezzling 
according to Healran's testimony.</i>

21:28.530 --> 21:31.430
<i>The mayor made a scene,</i>

21:31.430 --> 21:35.380
<i>but the only one who can win an 
argument against Papa is Mama, so...</i>

21:35.380 --> 21:37.390
That's enough! You're finished!

21:38.470 --> 21:43.060
<i>Now, one of Papa's trusty
 subordinates is supposed to come.</i>

21:43.300 --> 21:45.160
<i>Until then, the mayor</i>

21:45.160 --> 21:48.910
<i>is being held under the watch
of the adventurers' guild.</i>

21:49.210 --> 21:53.210
<i>And that takes care of the 
mayor's embezzlement schemes!</i>

21:53.210 --> 21:55.410
<i>Isn't that great, Healran?</i>

21:55.820 --> 21:58.080
<i>So now...</i>

21:58.080 --> 22:01.480
<i>I get to fully enjoy some well-deserved 
fluffy paradise time!</i>

23:35.100 --> 23:39.970
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.100 --> 23:39.970
<b>A Lot's Been Decided</b>
